<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Şahin Giray</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1745">1745</a>–<a href="/years/1787">1787</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Shahin Giray</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Şahin Giray was the last khan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimea">Crimea</a>, ruling from 1777 to 1783 with Russian support after the khanate became nominally independent in 1774. His centralising, European-style reforms of the army and administration provoked revolts that Russian troops put down. He abdicated after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catherine-the-great">Catherine II</a> annexed Crimea in 1783, moved to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> and was executed there on the sultan's orders in 1787.</p></div>
